 - Prevents endless todo lists from accumulating
 - Configurable via Account/Board settings
 
+### Stalled Cards
+
+Cards flag themselves as "stalled" when they drew a burst of attention and then went cold:
+- A burst is three or more comments from at least two different people landing on the card within a third of the board auto-postpone period, or someone being assigned to the card, or someone reopening it (`Card::Burst`)
+- Bursts are recorded in `cards.bursted_at` as activity happens and stick around; any activity on the card resets the stall
+- A bursted card that has been quiet for two weeks is stalled (`Card.stalled`, listed with `indexed_by=stalled`) and shows a "Stalled for" bubble wherever cards are shown
+
 ### UUID Primary Keys
 
 All tables use UUIDs (UUIDv7 format, base36-encoded as 25-char strings):
